  "flags": [
    "Section keys follow the MIF t6a.json unit ranges (F4101-04, F4201-04, F4301-06, F4401-04, F4501-03, F4690); the syllabus Program Analysis headers print them as F41ΧΧ / F42ΧΧ / F43ΧΧ / F44ΧΧ / F45ΧΧ (Greek capital chi) and F4690.",
    "Every Program Analysis maneuver in the Formation category sits under a 'Leader' or 'Wingman' sub-heading; the role is appended to 'name' (e.g. 'Formation approach (Leader)') because most maneuvers appear twice per section. 'verbatim' keeps the printed bullet exactly, without the role.",
    "Numbers are printed in a right-hand column (x≈397-439) aligned row-by-row with the bullets; alignment was resolved from PyMuPDF word coordinates, not from linear text extraction (linear extraction mis-groups them, e.g. 'Pitch out / Rejoin(4)(5)').",
    "per='section' for all entries: the Program Analysis numbers are totals for the whole Training Section (4-6 sorties). No Formation text defines a per-sortie minimum.",
    "F4301-06 p.214 prints 'Close Trail - Fighting Wing. (2) - (2)' — two numbers on one bullet (most plausibly Close Trail (2) and Fighting Wing (2)). Recorded as min_number 2; verbatim preserved.",
    "'Close Trail - Fighting Wing' spans two MIF rows (sn 22 'Close Trail' and sn 18 'Route / Fighting Wing'); mapped to sn 22.",
    "'Pitch out / Rejoin (5)' (Wingman, F41XX/F42XX/F43XX) has no single MIF row: it straddles sn 16 'Pitch Out / Spacing', sn 9 'Turning Rejoin' and sn 10 'Straight Ahead Rejoin'. mif_sn=null.",
    "Hook / Cross / Check turns all map to the single MIF row sn 28 'Cross/ Hook/ Shackle/ Check turns'; four distinct Program Analysis bullets share it.",
    "Syllabus prints 'Hook Turns' with Greek glyphs ('Ηοοκ'); 'name' is normalised to Latin 'Hook Turns', 'verbatim' keeps the printed Greek form.",
    "F4690 (Final Formation Checkride, pp.221-222) lists maneuvers with NO minimum numbers — maneuvers array intentionally empty.",
    "Mission table on p.207 labels the final checkride 'F4790', while the Program Analysis section header (p.221) and MIF t6a.json both use 'F4690'. Discrepancy in the source.",
    "PDF page 220 (printed -212-) is completely blank (no text, no images) between the F45XX and F4690 sections.",
    "special_instructions entries at page_pdf 210, 212 and 219 are section-level SPECIAL DIRECTIVES / RESTRICTIONS, not category Special Instructions; recorded with scope='category' because the schema offers only 'category|phase'. The p.212 instrument-approach directive is repeated verbatim in F43XX (p.214), F44XX (p.216) and F45XX (p.218).",
    "Section-level RESTRICTIONS blocks are recorded only when they add information not already carried by the category Special Instructions of p.207. Recorded: p.219 §3 (first SOLO of F45XX at F4501 per BD 3-1/HATC) — p.207 (3) covers only the 'same or next day' timing for F45XX. Excluded as redundant or non-informative: 'VMC in flight area' (pp.210, 212, 216, 219), 'Special instructions for the Formation Category apply' (pp.216, 219), and the p.214 F43XX restriction 'The first SOLO flight can be executed at the F4301, adhering to BD 3-1/HATC restrictions' (the F4301 designation is already stated in p.207 (3)). FUEL CONSUMPTION lines (600 LBS per sortie) are out of scope for minimums.",
    "The verbatim of special instruction (8) (p.207 Formation mission table) is a serialization of a printed table, not a literal line-by-line transcript: ' / ' separators between rows are inserted by this file and are NOT printed, and the two header lines ('DUAL   SOLO' and 'FORMATION CATEGORY | SECTION | SORTIES HOURS | SORTIES HOURS') are omitted. Column meaning of each pair of values is preserved in 'numbers' (sorties then hours, dual columns first, then solo). Hours are printed with a decimal comma in the source (4,8) and stored as decimal points (4.8).",
    "F44XX Leader lists no Delay 45° and no numbered Tactical Turns; F44XX/F45XX Leader 'Landing Pattern and Landing' and 'Tactical Turns' carry no number and are therefore not recorded."
  ]
}
